/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Treat the uncracked section as elastic.
   - P is the prestress in N; A the concrete area in mm²; e the eccentricity in mm; Zt, Zb the section moduli for the top and bottom fibres in mm³ (equal for a rectangle, bD²/6); M the moment in N·mm; f in N/mm².
   - Two stages are checked with this formula.
   - Think of the tendon force P as the tension T and the resultant concrete compression C = P as the other half of a couple.
   - a is the distance in mm from the tendon to the line of action of C; M is the load moment in N·mm; P the prestress in N.
   - The line traced by C along the span is the pressure line, or C-line.
   - A curved tendon presses up on the concrete along its whole length.
   - wp is the upward load in kN/m when P is in kN and e and L are in m.
   - If wp equals the downward load w, the beam carries only the axial P/A: no bending, no deflection.
*/
